url: "https://github.com/bioxcompute/dark-taxa-novelty"
keywords:
  - environmental DNA
  - novelty detection
  - 18S rRNA
  - open-set recognition
  - benchmark
abstract: >-
  1,760 marker-gene sequences from SILVA and PR2, split so that forty whole
  taxonomic groups are held out entirely, for measuring whether a model can
  recognise a taxon it has never seen. The baseline to beat is counting
  four-letter words against one centroid per reference group: AUC 0.7741 on
  full reads, 0.7578 at 512 bases and 0.7329 at 300 bases, measured by the
  sixty-line baseline.py in the same repository. Four published DNA foundation
  models do not beat it. Whole taxa are held out rather than random rows,
  because sequences within one taxon are not independent and a random split
  lets a model answer from memory and call it recognition.
